--TEST--
the registry is the whole roster of `Core`, so a member it does not hold is `E0405` wherever it is written — on an instance, on a class it states, and on a class it has never heard of (`rule:statements/static-is-a-member-modifier`, `rule:programs/no-runtime-autoload`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A registered class checked like any other: `Core\Uuid` states no `version`,
// and an instance is where its members are reached from. This used to type-check
// and then panic in `nvs-ir`, which had a call with no resolved target to lower.
Core\Uuid $id = Core\Uuid::v4();
echo $id->version(), "\n";
// The static half of the same question, for a class the registry does state.
echo Core\Uuid::variant($id), "\n";
// And a constant it does not state: `Core\Env` is a name `nvs_hir` resolves
// because nothing under `Core\` needs a declaration, which used to make every
// member of it trusted. The registry is the roster, and that class holds exactly
// the three constants spec § 15 names — so `SAPI`, which PHP has and Novis has
// no equivalent for, is knowably wrong here.
echo Core\Env::SAPI, "\n";
echo Core\Log::info("started"), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0405]: `Core\Uuid` has no method named `version`
%A
error[E0405]: `Core\Uuid` has no member named `variant`
%A
error[E0405]: `Core\Env` has no constant named `SAPI`
%A
error[E0405]: `Core\Log` has no member named `info`
%A
error: aborting due to 4 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
